<title>UK: Celltech seen getting boost from new drug.</title>
<headline>Celltech seen getting boost from new drug.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>British firm Celltech could achieve a major breakthrough in the UK biotechnology sector after German partner Bayer AG said a drug still under test would be launched next year, the Financial Times reported on Thursday.</p>
<p>The paper said the drug, codenamed BAYX 1351 at Celltech and called Norasept at Bayer, was a treatment for septic shock.</p>
<p>The drug had been in clinical trials for several years and the results of the final large-scale trial had been planned for the end of this month, the Financial Times said.</p>
<p>It said analysts had forecast Celltech's share price could rise to above 750 pence if the trial was successful. Celltech closed at 560p on Wednesday.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4366</p>
